Running tool mcp__PDE_modeling__generate_model({'specification': "Generate the Grad-Shafranov equilibrium PDE model for an axisymmetric tokamak plasma. The Grad-Shafranov equation describes the magnetohydrodynamic (MHD) equilibrium of the poloidal magnetic flux function psi(R,Z) in cylindrical (R,Z) coordinates. The equation is: R * d/dR( (1/R) * dpsi/dR ) + d^2 psi/dZ^2 = -mu0 * R^2 * dp/dpsi - F * dF/dpsi, where p(psi) is the plasma pressure profile and F(psi) = R*B_toroidal is the poloidal current function. Use standard profile choices (e.g., linear or Solov'ev-type source terms) so the right-hand side becomes an explicit function of R, Z, and psi. Include appropriate Dirichlet boundary conditions psi = 0 on the plasma boundary (a D-shaped or rectangular tokamak cross-section). Provide the strong form, weak form, and UFL representation suitable for a finite element discretization."})
Result of running tool {"request":"Generate the Grad-Shafranov equilibrium PDE model for an axisymmetric tokamak plasma. The Grad-Shafranov equation describes the magnetohydrodynamic (MHD) equilibrium of the poloidal magnetic flux function psi(R,Z) in cylindrical (R,Z) coordinates. The equation is: R * d/dR( (1/R) * dpsi/dR ) + d^2 psi/dZ^2 = -mu0 * R^2 * dp/dpsi - F * dF/dpsi, where p(psi) is the plasma pressure profile and F(psi) = R*B_toroidal is the poloidal current function. Use standard profile choices (e.g., linear or Solov'ev-type source terms) so the right-hand side becomes an explicit function of R, Z, and psi. Include appropriate Dirichlet boundary conditions psi = 0 on the plasma boundary (a D-shaped or rectangular tokamak cross-section). Provide the strong form, weak form, and UFL representation suitable for a finite element discretization.","time-dependent":false,"name":"Grad-Shafranov equation","full-response":"# Grad–Shafranov Equilibrium Model\n\nThe name of the PDE is [Grad-Shafranov equation].\n\nthe PDE is not time-dependent.\n\nBelow, the elliptic (Grad–Shafranov) operator is written as\n$\\Delta^\\* \\psi = R\\,\\partial_R\\!\\big(\\tfrac{1}{R}\\partial_R\\psi\\big) + \\partial_{ZZ}\\psi = \\partial_{RR}\\psi - \\tfrac{1}{R}\\partial_R\\psi + \\partial_{ZZ}\\psi$,\nand Solov'ev profiles are used so that $\\mu_0\\,dp/d\\psi = C_1$ (const) and $F\\,dF/d\\psi = C_2$ (const), giving the explicit source $f(R,Z,\\psi)=C_1 R^2 + C_2$ (general nonlinear source $f=\\mu_0 R^2 p'(\\psi)+F F'(\\psi)$ shown for completeness). The weak form is obtained by testing with $v/R$, which makes the operator self-adjoint with weight $1/R$.\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Grad-Shafranov Equilibrium PDE</title>\n<script>\n  window.MathJax = {\n    tex: { inlineMath: [['\\\\(','\\\\)']], displayMath: [['$$','$$'],['\\\\[','\\\\]']] }\n  };\n</script>\n<script src=\"https://polyfill.io/v3/polyfill.min.js?features=es6\"></script>\n<script id=\"MathJax-script\" async\n  src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\"></script>\n</head>\n<body>\n<h1>Grad&ndash;Shafranov Equilibrium of an Axisymmetric Tokamak</h1>\n\n<p>The name of the PDE is <strong>Grad&ndash;Shafranov equation</strong>.\nThe PDE is <strong>not time-dependent</strong> (it is an MHD equilibrium equation).</p>\n\n<h2>Grad&ndash;Shafranov operator</h2>\n<p>\n$$\n\\Delta^{*}\\psi \\;\\equiv\\; R\\,\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial R}\\!\\left(\\frac{1}{R}\\frac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial R}\\right)\n+ \\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial Z^{2}}\n\\;=\\; \\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial R^{2}} - \\frac{1}{R}\\frac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial R}\n+ \\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial Z^{2}}.\n$$\n</p>\n\n<h2>Strong form</h2>\n<p>Find the poloidal flux \\(\\psi(R,Z)\\) on the cross-section \\(\\Omega\\subset\\{R>0\\}\\) such that</p>\n<p>\n$$\n\\Delta^{*}\\psi\n= -\\,\\mu_{0}\\,R^{2}\\,\\frac{dp}{d\\psi} \\;-\\; F\\,\\frac{dF}{d\\psi}\n\\;\\equiv\\; -\\,f(R,Z,\\psi)\\qquad\\text{in }\\Omega,\n$$\n$$\n\\psi = 0 \\qquad\\text{on }\\partial\\Omega .\n$$\n</p>\n<p>With Solov'ev (linear) profiles \\( \\mu_{0}\\,dp/d\\psi = C_{1}\\), \\( F\\,dF/d\\psi = C_{2}\\):</p>\n<p>\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial R^{2}} - \\frac{1}{R}\\frac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial R}\n+ \\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial Z^{2}}\n= -\\left(C_{1}R^{2} + C_{2}\\right)\\quad\\text{in }\\Omega,\\qquad \\psi=0 \\text{ on } \\partial\\Omega .\n$$\n</p>\n\n<h2>Weak form</h2>\n<p>\nMultiply by \\(v/R\\) with \\(v\\in V_{0}=\\{v\\in H^{1}(\\Omega):v=0\\text{ on }\\partial\\Omega\\}\\),\nintegrate over \\(\\Omega\\) with \\(dx=dR\\,dZ\\), and integrate by parts. The weighted\nboundary terms vanish since \\(v=0\\) on \\(\\partial\\Omega\\). Find\n\\(\\psi\\in H^{1}(\\Omega)\\), \\(\\psi=0\\) on \\(\\partial\\Omega\\), such that for all \\(v\\in V_{0}\\):\n</p>\n<p>\n$$\n\\int_{\\Omega}\\frac{1}{R}\\,\\nabla\\psi\\cdot\\nabla v \\; dx\n=\\int_{\\Omega}\\frac{1}{R}\\,\\Big(\\mu_{0}R^{2}\\,p'(\\psi)+F(\\psi)F'(\\psi)\\Big)\\,v\\;dx .\n$$\n</p>\n<p>Solov'ev specialization (\\(f=C_{1}R^{2}+C_{2}\\)):</p>\n<p>\n$$\n\\int_{\\Omega}\\frac{1}{R}\\,\\nabla\\psi\\cdot\\nabla v \\; dx\n=\\int_{\\Omega}\\Big(C_{1}R+\\frac{C_{2}}{R}\\Big)\\,v\\;dx\n\\qquad\\forall v\\in V_{0}.\n$$\n</p>\n\n<h2>Domain (plasma boundary)</h2>\n<p>\nRectangular cross-section \\(\\Omega=[R_{\\mathrm{in}},R_{\\mathrm{out}}]\\times[Z_{\\min},Z_{\\max}]\\),\nor a D-shaped boundary (Miller parametrization)\n\\( R(\\theta)=R_{0}+a\\cos(\\theta+\\delta\\sin\\theta),\\; Z(\\theta)=\\kappa\\,a\\sin\\theta \\),\nwith minor radius \\(a\\), elongation \\(\\kappa\\), triangularity \\(\\delta\\); \\(\\psi=0\\) on this curve.\n</p>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n```latex\n% Grad-Shafranov equilibrium PDE (axisymmetric tokamak)\n% Name: Grad-Shafranov equation.  Time-dependent: NO (equilibrium).\n\n% Grad-Shafranov operator\n\\[\n\\Delta^{*}\\psi \\;\\equiv\\; R\\,\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial R}\\!\\left(\\frac{1}{R}\\frac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial R}\\right)\n+ \\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial Z^{2}}\n= \\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial R^{2}} - \\frac{1}{R}\\frac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial R}\n+ \\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial Z^{2}}.\n\\]\n\n% ---------- Strong form ----------\n% Find psi(R,Z) on Omega in {R>0}:\n\\[\n\\Delta^{*}\\psi\n= -\\,\\mu_{0}\\,R^{2}\\,\\frac{dp}{d\\psi} \\;-\\; F\\,\\frac{dF}{d\\psi}\n\\;\\equiv\\; -\\,f(R,Z,\\psi)\\qquad\\text{in }\\Omega,\n\\qquad \\psi = 0 \\ \\text{ on }\\ \\partial\\Omega .\n\\]\n\n% Solov'ev (linear) profiles:  mu0 dp/dpsi = C1,  F dF/dpsi = C2\n\\[\n\\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial R^{2}} - \\frac{1}{R}\\frac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial R}\n+ \\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial Z^{2}}\n= -\\left(C_{1}R^{2} + C_{2}\\right)\\quad\\text{in }\\Omega,\n\\qquad \\psi=0 \\ \\text{ on }\\ \\partial\\Omega .\n\\]\n\n% ---------- Weak form ----------\n% Test with v/R, v in V0 = { v in H^1(Omega) : v = 0 on dOmega }, dx = dR dZ.\n\\[\n\\int_{\\Omega}\\frac{1}{R}\\,\\nabla\\psi\\cdot\\nabla v \\; dx\n=\\int_{\\Omega}\\frac{1}{R}\\,\\Big(\\mu_{0}R^{2}\\,p'(\\psi)+F(\\psi)F'(\\psi)\\Big)\\,v\\;dx\n\\qquad\\forall\\, v\\in V_{0}.\n\\]\n\n% Solov'ev specialization ( f = C1 R^2 + C2 ):\n\\[\n\\int_{\\Omega}\\frac{1}{R}\\,\\nabla\\psi\\cdot\\nabla v \\; dx\n=\\int_{\\Omega}\\Big(C_{1}R+\\frac{C_{2}}{R}\\Big)\\,v\\;dx\n\\qquad\\forall\\, v\\in V_{0}.\n\\]\n\n% Boundary / domain:\n% Rectangular:  Omega = [R_in, R_out] x [Z_min, Z_max].\n% D-shaped (Miller):  R = R0 + a cos(theta + delta sin theta),  Z = kappa a sin theta.\n```\n\n```python\n# Grad-Shafranov equilibrium in an axisymmetric tokamak (FEniCS / UFL)\n# Name: Grad-Shafranov equation.   Time-dependent: NO (steady equilibrium).\n#\n# Weak form (weight 1/R):\n#   Find psi in V, psi = 0 on dOmega, such that for all v in V0:\n#     integral( (1/R) * dot(grad(psi), grad(v)) ) dx\n#       = integral( (1/R) * f(R,Z,psi) * v ) dx\n#   with f = mu0 * R^2 * p'(psi) + F(psi)*F'(psi)   (general)\n#        f = C1 * R^2 + C2                           (Solov'ev, linear)\n\nfrom fenics import *\n\n# ---- Domain: rectangular tokamak cross-section (R>0) ----\nR_in, R_out = 0.5, 1.5\nZ_min, Z_max = -1.0, 1.0\nmesh = RectangleMesh(Point(R_in, Z_min), Point(R_out, Z_max), 96, 96)\n# (For a D-shaped boundary, build the mesh with mshr from the Miller curve\n#  R = R0 + a*cos(t + delta*sin t), Z = kappa*a*sin t, and impose psi=0 on it.)\n\n# ---- Function space and Dirichlet BC: psi = 0 on the plasma boundary ----\nV  = FunctionSpace(mesh, \"P\", 1)\nbc = DirichletBC(V, Constant(0.0), \"on_boundary\")\n\n# ---- Coordinates and Solov'ev source coefficients ----\nxR = SpatialCoordinate(mesh)\nR, Z = xR[0], xR[1]\n\nmu0 = Constant(4.0e-7 * pi)   # vacuum permeability\nC1  = Constant(1.0)           # mu0 * dp/dpsi   (constant)  -> Solov'ev\nC2  = Constant(1.0)           # F * dF/dpsi     (constant)  -> Solov'ev\n\n# Explicit Solov'ev source f(R,Z,psi) = C1 R^2 + C2  (independent of psi -> linear)\ndef f_source(psi):\n    return C1 * R**2 + C2\n    # General nonlinear profiles instead would read, e.g.:\n    #   dp_dpsi = ...(psi);  FdF = ...(psi)\n    #   return mu0 * R**2 * dp_dpsi + FdF\n\n# ================= UFL: linear (Solov'ev) formulation =================\npsi = TrialFunction(V)\nv   = TestFunction(V)\n\na = (1.0 / R) * dot(grad(psi), grad(v)) * dx           # bilinear form\nL = (1.0 / R) * f_source(psi=None) * v * dx            # linear form (f indep. of psi)\n\npsi_h = Function(V, name=\"psi\")\nsolve(a == L, psi_h, bc)\n\n# ============ UFL: general nonlinear residual (if f = f(psi)) ============\n# psi_n = Function(V, name=\"psi\")\n# v     = TestFunction(V)\n# F_res = (1.0 / R) * dot(grad(psi_n), grad(v)) * dx \\\n#       - (1.0 / R) * f_source(psi_n) * v * dx\n# solve(F_res == 0, psi_n, bc)\n```","html":"\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Grad-Shafranov Equilibrium PDE</title>\n<script>\n  window.MathJax = {\n    tex: { inlineMath: [['\\\\(','\\\\)']], displayMath: [['$$','$$'],['\\\\[','\\\\]']] }\n  };\n</script>\n<script src=\"https://polyfill.io/v3/polyfill.min.js?features=es6\"></script>\n<script id=\"MathJax-script\" async\n  src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\"></script>\n</head>\n<body>\n<h1>Grad&ndash;Shafranov Equilibrium of an Axisymmetric Tokamak</h1>\n\n<p>The name of the PDE is <strong>Grad&ndash;Shafranov equation</strong>.\nThe PDE is <strong>not time-dependent</strong> (it is an MHD equilibrium equation).</p>\n\n<h2>Grad&ndash;Shafranov operator</h2>\n<p>\n$$\n\\Delta^{*}\\psi \\;\\equiv\\; R\\,\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial R}\\!\\left(\\frac{1}{R}\\frac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial R}\\right)\n+ \\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial Z^{2}}\n\\;=\\; \\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial R^{2}} - \\frac{1}{R}\\frac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial R}\n+ \\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial Z^{2}}.\n$$\n</p>\n\n<h2>Strong form</h2>\n<p>Find the poloidal flux \\(\\psi(R,Z)\\) on the cross-section \\(\\Omega\\subset\\{R>0\\}\\) such that</p>\n<p>\n$$\n\\Delta^{*}\\psi\n= -\\,\\mu_{0}\\,R^{2}\\,\\frac{dp}{d\\psi} \\;-\\; F\\,\\frac{dF}{d\\psi}\n\\;\\equiv\\; -\\,f(R,Z,\\psi)\\qquad\\text{in }\\Omega,\n$$\n$$\n\\psi = 0 \\qquad\\text{on }\\partial\\Omega .\n$$\n</p>\n<p>With Solov'ev (linear) profiles \\( \\mu_{0}\\,dp/d\\psi = C_{1}\\), \\( F\\,dF/d\\psi = C_{2}\\):</p>\n<p>\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial R^{2}} - \\frac{1}{R}\\frac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial R}\n+ \\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial Z^{2}}\n= -\\left(C_{1}R^{2} + C_{2}\\right)\\quad\\text{in }\\Omega,\\qquad \\psi=0 \\text{ on } \\partial\\Omega .\n$$\n</p>\n\n<h2>Weak form</h2>\n<p>\nMultiply by \\(v/R\\) with \\(v\\in V_{0}=\\{v\\in H^{1}(\\Omega):v=0\\text{ on }\\partial\\Omega\\}\\),\nintegrate over \\(\\Omega\\) with \\(dx=dR\\,dZ\\), and integrate by parts. The weighted\nboundary terms vanish since \\(v=0\\) on \\(\\partial\\Omega\\). Find\n\\(\\psi\\in H^{1}(\\Omega)\\), \\(\\psi=0\\) on \\(\\partial\\Omega\\), such that for all \\(v\\in V_{0}\\):\n</p>\n<p>\n$$\n\\int_{\\Omega}\\frac{1}{R}\\,\\nabla\\psi\\cdot\\nabla v \\; dx\n=\\int_{\\Omega}\\frac{1}{R}\\,\\Big(\\mu_{0}R^{2}\\,p'(\\psi)+F(\\psi)F'(\\psi)\\Big)\\,v\\;dx .\n$$\n</p>\n<p>Solov'ev specialization (\\(f=C_{1}R^{2}+C_{2}\\)):</p>\n<p>\n$$\n\\int_{\\Omega}\\frac{1}{R}\\,\\nabla\\psi\\cdot\\nabla v \\; dx\n=\\int_{\\Omega}\\Big(C_{1}R+\\frac{C_{2}}{R}\\Big)\\,v\\;dx\n\\qquad\\forall v\\in V_{0}.\n$$\n</p>\n\n<h2>Domain (plasma boundary)</h2>\n<p>\nRectangular cross-section \\(\\Omega=[R_{\\mathrm{in}},R_{\\mathrm{out}}]\\times[Z_{\\min},Z_{\\max}]\\),\nor a D-shaped boundary (Miller parametrization)\n\\( R(\\theta)=R_{0}+a\\cos(\\theta+\\delta\\sin\\theta),\\; Z(\\theta)=\\kappa\\,a\\sin\\theta \\),\nwith minor radius \\(a\\), elongation \\(\\kappa\\), triangularity \\(\\delta\\); \\(\\psi=0\\) on this curve.\n</p>\n</body>\n</html>\n","latex":"\n% Grad-Shafranov equilibrium PDE (axisymmetric tokamak)\n% Name: Grad-Shafranov equation.  Time-dependent: NO (equilibrium).\n\n% Grad-Shafranov operator\n\\[\n\\Delta^{*}\\psi \\;\\equiv\\; R\\,\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial R}\\!\\left(\\frac{1}{R}\\frac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial R}\\right)\n+ \\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial Z^{2}}\n= \\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial R^{2}} - \\frac{1}{R}\\frac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial R}\n+ \\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial Z^{2}}.\n\\]\n\n% ---------- Strong form ----------\n% Find psi(R,Z) on Omega in {R>0}:\n\\[\n\\Delta^{*}\\psi\n= -\\,\\mu_{0}\\,R^{2}\\,\\frac{dp}{d\\psi} \\;-\\; F\\,\\frac{dF}{d\\psi}\n\\;\\equiv\\; -\\,f(R,Z,\\psi)\\qquad\\text{in }\\Omega,\n\\qquad \\psi = 0 \\ \\text{ on }\\ \\partial\\Omega .\n\\]\n\n% Solov'ev (linear) profiles:  mu0 dp/dpsi = C1,  F dF/dpsi = C2\n\\[\n\\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial R^{2}} - \\frac{1}{R}\\frac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial R}\n+ \\frac{\\partial^{2}\\psi}{\\partial Z^{2}}\n= -\\left(C_{1}R^{2} + C_{2}\\right)\\quad\\text{in }\\Omega,\n\\qquad \\psi=0 \\ \\text{ on }\\ \\partial\\Omega .\n\\]\n\n% ---------- Weak form ----------\n% Test with v/R, v in V0 = { v in H^1(Omega) : v = 0 on dOmega }, dx = dR dZ.\n\\[\n\\int_{\\Omega}\\frac{1}{R}\\,\\nabla\\psi\\cdot\\nabla v \\; dx\n=\\int_{\\Omega}\\frac{1}{R}\\,\\Big(\\mu_{0}R^{2}\\,p'(\\psi)+F(\\psi)F'(\\psi)\\Big)\\,v\\;dx\n\\qquad\\forall\\, v\\in V_{0}.\n\\]\n\n% Solov'ev specialization ( f = C1 R^2 + C2 ):\n\\[\n\\int_{\\Omega}\\frac{1}{R}\\,\\nabla\\psi\\cdot\\nabla v \\; dx\n=\\int_{\\Omega}\\Big(C_{1}R+\\frac{C_{2}}{R}\\Big)\\,v\\;dx\n\\qquad\\forall\\, v\\in V_{0}.\n\\]\n\n% Boundary / domain:\n% Rectangular:  Omega = [R_in, R_out] x [Z_min, Z_max].\n% D-shaped (Miller):  R = R0 + a cos(theta + delta sin theta),  Z = kappa a sin theta.\n","python":"\n# Grad-Shafranov equilibrium in an axisymmetric tokamak (FEniCS / UFL)\n# Name: Grad-Shafranov equation.   Time-dependent: NO (steady equilibrium).\n#\n# Weak form (weight 1/R):\n#   Find psi in V, psi = 0 on dOmega, such that for all v in V0:\n#     integral( (1/R) * dot(grad(psi), grad(v)) ) dx\n#       = integral( (1/R) * f(R,Z,psi) * v ) dx\n#   with f = mu0 * R^2 * p'(psi) + F(psi)*F'(psi)   (general)\n#        f = C1 * R^2 + C2                           (Solov'ev, linear)\n\nfrom fenics import *\n\n# ---- Domain: rectangular tokamak cross-section (R>0) ----\nR_in, R_out = 0.5, 1.5\nZ_min, Z_max = -1.0, 1.0\nmesh = RectangleMesh(Point(R_in, Z_min), Point(R_out, Z_max), 96, 96)\n# (For a D-shaped boundary, build the mesh with mshr from the Miller curve\n#  R = R0 + a*cos(t + delta*sin t), Z = kappa*a*sin t, and impose psi=0 on it.)\n\n# ---- Function space and Dirichlet BC: psi = 0 on the plasma boundary ----\nV  = FunctionSpace(mesh, \"P\", 1)\nbc = DirichletBC(V, Constant(0.0), \"on_boundary\")\n\n# ---- Coordinates and Solov'ev source coefficients ----\nxR = SpatialCoordinate(mesh)\nR, Z = xR[0], xR[1]\n\nmu0 = Constant(4.0e-7 * pi)   # vacuum permeability\nC1  = Constant(1.0)           # mu0 * dp/dpsi   (constant)  -> Solov'ev\nC2  = Constant(1.0)           # F * dF/dpsi     (constant)  -> Solov'ev\n\n# Explicit Solov'ev source f(R,Z,psi) = C1 R^2 + C2  (independent of psi -> linear)\ndef f_source(psi):\n    return C1 * R**2 + C2\n    # General nonlinear profiles instead would read, e.g.:\n    #   dp_dpsi = ...(psi);  FdF = ...(psi)\n    #   return mu0 * R**2 * dp_dpsi + FdF\n\n# ================= UFL: linear (Solov'ev) formulation =================\npsi = TrialFunction(V)\nv   = TestFunction(V)\n\na = (1.0 / R) * dot(grad(psi), grad(v)) * dx           # bilinear form\nL = (1.0 / R) * f_source(psi=None) * v * dx            # linear form (f indep. of psi)\n\npsi_h = Function(V, name=\"psi\")\nsolve(a == L, psi_h, bc)\n\n# ============ UFL: general nonlinear residual (if f = f(psi)) ============\n# psi_n = Function(V, name=\"psi\")\n# v     = TestFunction(V)\n# F_res = (1.0 